    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing OCR Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Vision AI for the OCR task. I'll need to figure out how to integrate it cleanly into the `extract_text.py` script, ensuring the provider is easily identifiable within the code for potential future modifications. This should allow a straightforward adaptation to other OCR providers if needed.\n\n\n**Implementing OCR Workflow**\n\nI'm now focusing on the Python script, `extract_text.py`, and how to best integrate Google Cloud Vision AI. The primary goal is to make the OCR provider easily swappable, so I'm thinking of how to best signal the provider in the code. I'm aiming for easy adaptability to other providers in the future. I'll need to use and identify `google.cloud.vision_v1` and `ImageAnnotatorClient`.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867568226,
          "start": 1789867566805
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc6ba6d5001TufwukvNJhFuki",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc6ba0f5001t4Pd2o0cS53ixH",
      "session_id": "ses_f43945f87ffeFTN3p90B22q4lo",
      "time_created": 1789867566805,
      "time_updated": 1789867568226
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "RLFJvlGlpGDUXYOd",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import vision\n\ndef extract_text_from_image(image_content: bytes) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts plain text from a scanned document image using Google Cloud Vision AI.\n\n    Args:\n        image_content: The content of the image file as bytes.\n\n    Returns:\n        The extracted plain text from the image.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = vision.ImageAnnotatorClient()\n    image = vision.Image(content=image_content)\n\n    response = client.text_detection(image=image)\n    texts = response.text_annotations\n\n    if texts:\n        # The first text annotation is the full text of the document\n        full_text = texts[0].description\n        return full_text\n    else:\n        return \"\"\n\n",
            "filePath": "extract_text.py"
          },
